record legeos.observation.freeze-watchdog-not-deployed-20261001/1 : observation {
    title "After the 2026-10-01 freezes the evidence harness is armed on the laptop but the installed templar-comp still has no watchdog"
    state superseded
    statement """
        Read from Lubuntu on 2026-10-01 against the TemplarOS root (/media/dk/templaros-root, journal @var/log/journal/13ddaed3..., readable via its ACL). Boot fbbc3d53 (2026-10-01 08:38-11:45 UTC) did not freeze: a logout at 09:04:24 (shell-initiated session restart) and a power-key poweroff at 11:45:30 after the user ran apt in kitty at 11:43:56-11:44:23, after a clean wake from a 900 s idle blank at 11:43:33. Armed on the installed root: /usr/lib/sysctl.d/60-templaros-hang-evidence.conf, /usr/lib/systemd/journald.conf.d/60-templaros.conf, coredump.conf.d/templaros.conf, systemd-coredump, dk in adm; ~/.config/systemd/user/templar-comp.service.d/watchdog-abort.conf sets TEMPLAR_COMP_WATCHDOG_ABORT_AFTER_SECS=30. Not deployed: /usr/bin/templar-comp is dated 2026-09-30 and contains no watchdog strings (only sd_notify WATCHDOG=), so the drop-in is inert and the next freeze on this build leaves no compositor-side evidence. /var/lib/systemd/coredump and pstore are empty. Freeze boots -7 (c412a890) and -3 (54b1efc8) both log smithay 'surface missing from known popups' as templar-comp's last line; in -3 sudo apt commands ran at 06:39:14-32 UTC, after that last line, so the compositor's last log line does not mark the freeze onset. Working tree at this commit: cargo test -p templar-comp 156 passed, cargo test -p templar freeze 13 passed.
        """
    observed_at git:50af3784cb5c3f0ebe72a1e15f12a88f57e11290
    method command
    watches [
        "compositor/templar-comp/src/watchdog.rs",
        "compositor/templar-comp/src/backend/udev.rs",
        "session/units/user/templar-comp.service"
    ]
    derived_from [ @legeos.observation.desktop-freezes-20261001-compositor-main-thread-blocked ]
    author "dk"
}

